ALTCPM and ZXCPM related tools

The kits require a command line CP/M emulator.

BASCOM-ALTCPM-XDEV.ZIP works also in ZXBASIC mode but needs the z88dk/support/rel/rebase.c program.

The BDS C kit is a beefed setup built around the original ALTCPM base libraries and compiler. 
It should, at some extent, permit to build historical programs which hardly could be built natively
on an ALTCPM system. Also the library is slightly extended, still trying to keep it compatible 
with CP/M 1.4
